  "articleBody": "When you're trying to fix a drywall issue, it's easy to fall into some common traps that end up making things worse. One of the biggest mistakes is patching over an unresolved leak. You absolutely have to find and fix the source of the water damage first, otherwise, you're just putting a band-aid on a bigger problem. Another blunder is not letting the joint compound dry properly between coats. Rushing this step will lead to cracks, uneven surfaces, and a repair that just won’t last. For larger holes, not using enough backing or tape is a big no-no; your patch needs proper support to stay strong and seamless. And then there's texture and paint matching – often overlooked, but crucial for an invisible repair. If your patch doesn't blend perfectly with the existing wall texture and paint sheen, it'll stick out like a sore thumb. Remember, a little patience and attention to detail go a long way. If the repair seems too complex, or you’re worried about making these mistakes, HH Remodeling LLC is here to help folks in the Denver area. We know how to get it right the first time.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
